Agent 7.81.0 shipped http_check 12.7.x, which added an `http_status_code` tag to `network.http.can_connect`, `network.http.cant_connect` and `network.http.response_time` unconditionally. That split each metric into one context per status code and changed how existing monitors evaluate, so it is rolled back here: by default no tag is added and the metric contexts match those from before 12.7.0. A single `http_outcome` tag is available behind the new `enable_http_outcome_tag` option instead. It carries the HTTP status code of the response, or, on `network.http.can_connect` and `network.http.cant_connect` when no response was received, one of `ssl_error`, `timeout`, `connection_error` or `socket_error`.
